What are Car Seat Adjustment Motors?
Car seat adjustment motors are precision electromechanical components that enable power-assisted positioning of vehicle seats. These compact yet powerful actuators convert electrical energy into controlled mechanical movement through either rotary or linear motion. Operating on standard 12V or advanced 48V vehicle electrical systems, they're integrated with position sensors and electronic control units to enable sophisticated functions including:
•	8-12 way power seat adjustments (forward/backward, height, tilt, recline)
•	Memory seating presets with driver recognition
•	Automated entry/exit positioning
•	Dynamic lumbar support adjustment
